 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\nActivities\n\nTo simulate rate steps, access billing in the simulation mode or perform periodic billing with integrated budget billing simulation.\nYou access the transaction for individual billing simulation in the SAP menu under |}Utilities Industry \u00bb Billing \u00bb Billing Execution\nIndividual Processing \u00bb Individual Simulation \u00bb Billing\n\ni Note\n\nTo ensure simulation is as accurate as possible, note the following:\n\ne Inthe time-of-use interface, use a consumption pattern (and a synthetic profile) that best suits the customer\nconsumption situation.\n\ne Enter the period consumption for interval meters during move-in.\ne Enter a percentage minimum share that is as large as possible in the rate.\n\ne If you create a contract in a vacant status period, for example, with the owner of a rented apartment, we recommend\nthat you implement BAdI ISU_LFASTEDM_TOU_SIMULATION, method DETERMINE_CONTRACTS.\n\nMore Information\n\nFor more information about the simulation process flow, see the system documentation TOU Simulation, which you can access\nfrom a link in the description of the field Consumption Pattern (F1 Help) in the time-of-use interface.\n\nBusiness Function Utilities, Advanced Metering Infrastructure 4 (ISU AMI_4)\n\nTechnical Reference\n\nThis section describes the technical requirements for contract billing based on profile values in an MDUS system:\n\ne Business Function:\n\nThe business function Advanced Metering Infrastructure 2 (ISU _AMI_ 2) is active.\n\ne Enterprise Services for MDUS Request:\n\no UtilitiesTimeSeriesCalculationERPBulkCreateRequest Out transfers the request items to the\nMDUS system.\n\no UtilitiesTimeSeriesCalculationERPBulkCreateConfirmation In sends the results of the request\nitems back to the SAP system.\n\no UtilitiesTimeSeriesCalculationERPCancellationBulkRequest_ Out repeats the MDUS request.\nThat is, it reverses an existing request and sends a new one.\n\ne Business Add-Ins (BAdlIs):\no ISU _MDUS_ FORMULA enables additional consistency checks for the time-of-use formula.\n\no ISU MDUS_IFACE enables additional consistency checks for the time-of-use interface.\n\nTCI AARNITIC mn rmemere _._LcI.. ...Le eeLt yg. gp. ppv~ryrim@m ._._....__g \u00a2.. Lit] LI Ll...) nee ee Bw eke 8g Od ee ce ee ee\n",
